            <span id="alg1.l27.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span><math id="alg1.l27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{Rebranch}(j,\kappa_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">Rebranch</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{Rebranch}(j,\kappa_{j})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l27.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> 
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l28" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">28:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l28.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span><math id="alg1.l28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{Repair}(j,i,\kappa_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">Repair</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{Repair}(j,i,\kappa_{j})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l28.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> 
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l29" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">29:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l29.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">end</span><span id="alg1.l29.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="alg1.l29.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">while</span><span id="alg1.l29.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l30" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">30:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l30.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">return</span><span id="alg1.l30.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Best plan found in </span><math id="alg1.l30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l30.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> based on cost
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l31" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">31:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l31.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">   </span><span id="alg1.l31.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;float:right;"><span id="alg1.l31.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">// Timeout or failure</span>
</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Planner State and Initialization:</span> The search state is represented by nodes <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}</annotation></semantics></math> in a search tree, each corresponding to a tuple of selected plan indices <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{b}=(b_{1},\dots,b_{N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒃</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{b}=(b_{1},\dots,b_{N})</annotation></semantics></math>. An index <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i}\in\{1,\dots,B\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i}\in\{1,\dots,B\}</annotation></semantics></math> points to a candidate delta-action sequence <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\bm{q}_{i}^{b_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>i</mi><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\bm{q}_{i}^{b_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> for arm <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, covering a prediction horizon <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{p}</annotation></semantics></math>. The search maintains a frontier set <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math>, implemented as a min-priority queue storing nodes <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}</annotation></semantics></math> ordered by a cost function <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(\mathcal{N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(\mathcal{N})</annotation></semantics></math> guiding the search towards promising nodes. This cost estimates solution quality by combining path smoothness, goal proximity and penalty for collisions. Initially, each arm <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> uses its single-arm model <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\epsilon}_{\theta_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\epsilon}_{\theta_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> conditioned on its observation history <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{o}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{o}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> of up to <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{o}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{o}</annotation></semantics></math> steps in the past to sample <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> diverse candidate delta-action sequences <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{i}=\{\Delta\bm{q}_{i}^{1},\dots,\Delta\bm{q}_{i}^{B}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{i}=\{\Delta\bm{q}_{i}^{1},\dots,\Delta\bm{q}_{i}^{B}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. The search begins with a root node <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> placed in <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> along with an empty set of conflicting plan indices (<math id="S3.SS3.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}</annotation></semantics></math>) that will be updated upon expansions. A collision cache <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> stores pairwise collision check results.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.SS3.fig2" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_figure_panel ltx_float_algorithm ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle ltx_framed ltx_framed_top" style="width:165.6pt;">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> Generate Successors by Rebranch</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
                
                
              <span id="alg2.l1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> <math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{ego}\text{ arm},\text{conflicts }\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ego</mtext><mtext> arm</mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mtext>conflicts </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{ego}\text{ arm},\text{conflicts }\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
                
                
              <span id="alg2.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=1\dotsc|\mathcal{P}_{\texttt{ego}}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ego</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=1\dotsc|\mathcal{P}_{\texttt{ego}}|</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
                
                
                <span id="alg2.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\notin\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\notin\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
                
                
                 <math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{\texttt{ego}}^{\text{new}}\leftarrow m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ego</mtext><mtext>new</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{\texttt{ego}}^{\text{new}}\leftarrow m</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
                
                
                 <math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{b}^{\prime}\leftarrow(b_{1},\dotsc,b_{\texttt{ego}}^{\text{new}},\dotsc,b_{N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝒃</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ego</mtext><mtext>new</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{b}^{\prime}\leftarrow(b_{1},\dotsc,b_{\texttt{ego}}^{\text{new}},\dotsc,b_{N})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
                
                
                 <math id="alg2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}^{\prime}\leftarrow\texttt{Node}(\bm{b}=\bm{b}^{\prime},\mathcal{K}=\kappa)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Node</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒃</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝒃</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}^{\prime}\leftarrow\texttt{Node}(\bm{b}=\bm{b}^{\prime},\mathcal{K}=\kappa)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
                
                
                 <math id="alg2.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}.\texttt{Insert}(\mathcal{N}^{\prime},g(\mathcal{N}^{\prime}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Insert</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}.\texttt{Insert}(\mathcal{N}^{\prime},g(\mathcal{N}^{\prime}))</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
                
                
                <span id="alg2.l8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
                
                
              <span id="alg2.l9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="alg3" class="ltx_float ltx_figure_panel ltx_float_algorithm ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle ltx_framed ltx_framed_top" style="width:165.6pt;">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 3</span> </span> Generate Successors by Repair</figcaption>
<div id="alg3.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg3.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
                
                
              <span id="alg3.l1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> 
<span id="alg3.l1.3" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:150.6pt;">
<span id="alg3.l1.3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="alg3.l1.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">ego</span> arm, <span id="alg3.l1.3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">other</span> arm, conflicts <math id="alg3.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>,</span>
<span id="alg3.l1.3.2" class="ltx_p">Model <math id="alg3.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\epsilon}_{\theta_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\epsilon}_{\theta_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
                
                
              <math id="alg3.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\bm{o}}_{\texttt{ego}}\leftarrow\texttt{GetPairedObs}(\texttt{ego},\texttt{other})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒐</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ego</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">GetPairedObs</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ego</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">other</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\bm{o}}_{\texttt{ego}}\leftarrow\texttt{GetPairedObs}(\texttt{ego},\texttt{other})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
                
                
              Sample <math id="alg3.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\Delta\bm{q}_{\texttt{ego}}^{\text{new},m}\}_{m=1}^{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ego</mtext><mrow><mtext>new</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\Delta\bm{q}_{\texttt{ego}}^{\text{new},m}\}_{m=1}^{B}</annotation></semantics></math> using <math id="alg3.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\epsilon}_{\theta_{2}}(\hat{\bm{o}}_{\texttt{ego}},\cdot,\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒐</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ego</mtext></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\epsilon}_{\theta_{2}}(\hat{\bm{o}}_{\texttt{ego}},\cdot,\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
                
                
              <span id="alg3.l4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg3.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=1\dotsc B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=1\dotsc B</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg3.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
                
                
                <math id="alg3.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{\texttt{ego}}^{\text{new}}\leftarrow\mathcal{P}_{\texttt{ego}}.\texttt{Update}(\Delta\bm{q}_{\texttt{ego}}^{\text{new},m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ego</mtext><mtext>new</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ego</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Update</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ego</mtext><mrow><mtext>new</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{\texttt{ego}}^{\text{new}}\leftarrow\mathcal{P}_{\texttt{ego}}.\texttt{Update}(\Delta\bm{q}_{\texttt{ego}}^{\text{new},m})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
                
                
                <math id="alg3.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{b}^{\prime}\leftarrow(b_{1},\dotsc,b_{\texttt{ego}}^{\text{new}},\dotsc,b_{N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝒃</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ego</mtext><mtext>new</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{b}^{\prime}\leftarrow(b_{1},\dotsc,b_{\texttt{ego}}^{\text{new}},\dotsc,b_{N})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
                
                
                <math id="alg3.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}^{\prime}\leftarrow(\bm{b}=\bm{b}^{\prime},\mathcal{K}=\kappa)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒃</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝒃</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}^{\prime}\leftarrow(\bm{b}=\bm{b}^{\prime},\mathcal{K}=\kappa)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
                
                
                <math id="alg3.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}.\texttt{Insert}(\mathcal{N}^{\prime},g(\mathcal{N}^{\prime}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Insert</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}.\texttt{Insert}(\mathcal{N}^{\prime},g(\mathcal{N}^{\prime}))</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
                
                
              <span id="alg3.l9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg3.l9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure></div></div>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Search Process and Conflict Resolution:</span> The main loop (lines <a href="#alg1.l14" title="In Algorithm 1 ‣ 3.3 Diffusion-Guided Multi-Arm Planning (DG-MAP) ‣ 3 Approach ‣ Diffusion-Guided Multi-Arm Motion Planning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>-<a href="#alg1.l29" title="In Algorithm 1 ‣ 3.3 Diffusion-Guided Multi-Arm Planning (DG-MAP) ‣ 3 Approach ‣ Diffusion-Guided Multi-Arm Motion Planning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>) iteratively extracts the lowest-cost node <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math>. It checks the corresponding plan combination for collisions using <span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FindFirstCollision</span> (line <a href="#alg1.l17" title="In Algorithm 1 ‣ 3.3 Diffusion-Guided Multi-Arm Planning (DG-MAP) ‣ 3 Approach ‣ Diffusion-Guided Multi-Arm Motion Planning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>). If no conflict is found, a valid solution is returned (line <a href="#alg1.l18" title="In Algorithm 1 ‣ 3.3 Diffusion-Guided Multi-Arm Planning (DG-MAP) ‣ 3 Approach ‣ Diffusion-Guided Multi-Arm Motion Planning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">As the node <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}</annotation></semantics></math> is expanded we detect a conflict <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=(i,j,\hat{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=(i,j,\hat{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is the earliest time step within the prediction horizon <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> where the plans <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\bm{q}_{i}^{b_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>i</mi><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\bm{q}_{i}^{b_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\bm{q}_{j}^{b_{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>j</mi><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\bm{q}_{j}^{b_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math> collide. <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is the earliest conflict time and is updated based on <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. It signifies that the current combination of plans is collision-free up to time <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{*}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{*}-1</annotation></semantics></math>, which could potentially allow for safe partial execution in a receding horizon context, although our primary goal here is to find a fully collision-free plan for the horizon <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{p}</annotation></semantics></math>. The set of conflicts <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> indicate the plan indices corresponding to arm <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> that have been found to be in conflict in the ancestors of the node. This book-keeping helps in avoiding redundant plans that did not succeed in earlier expansions. The node expansion generates successor nodes by exploring alternatives for the conflicting arms <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> using two distinct strategies (lines <a href="#alg1.l24" title="In Algorithm 1 ‣ 3.3 Diffusion-Guided Multi-Arm Planning (DG-MAP) ‣ 3 Approach ‣ Diffusion-Guided Multi-Arm Motion Planning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>-<a href="#alg1.l28" title="In Algorithm 1 ‣ 3.3 Diffusion-Guided Multi-Arm Planning (DG-MAP) ‣ 3 Approach ‣ Diffusion-Guided Multi-Arm Motion Planning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>). First, <span id="S3.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Rebranch</span> (Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ 3.3 Diffusion-Guided Multi-Arm Planning (DG-MAP) ‣ 3 Approach ‣ Diffusion-Guided Multi-Arm Motion Planning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) creates successors by trying alternative, pre-existing plans from <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math> for both <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>. Second, <span id="S3.SS3.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Repair</span> (Algorithm <a href="#alg3" title="Algorithm 3 ‣ 3.3 Diffusion-Guided Multi-Arm Planning (DG-MAP) ‣ 3 Approach ‣ Diffusion-Guided Multi-Arm Motion Planning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) uses the dual-arm model <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\epsilon}_{\theta_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\epsilon}_{\theta_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> to generate <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> new candidate sequences for both <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>, specifically aiming to avoid the detected conflict <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>, and creates successors for each successful repair. All generated successors are added to <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math>, allowing the search to explore other alternatives based on their estimated costs.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Termination:</span> The search continues until a collision-free node is extracted or termination conditions (timeout or empty frontier) are met, returning the best plan found.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">DG-MAP (Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 3.3 Diffusion-Guided Multi-Arm Planning (DG-MAP) ‣ 3 Approach ‣ Diffusion-Guided Multi-Arm Motion Planning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) operates within a closed-loop, receding horizon controller (Figure <a href="#S3.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 3 Approach ‣ Diffusion-Guided Multi-Arm Motion Planning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>). At each step, it plans from the current state, returning action sequences <math id="S3.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\Delta\bm{q}_{i}^{b_{i}}\}_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>i</mi><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\Delta\bm{q}_{i}^{b_{i}}\}_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> for horizon <math id="S3.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> and the predicted collision-free duration <math id="S3.SS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{*}\leq T_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{*}\leq T_{p}</annotation></semantics></math>. Actions are executed for <math id="S3.SS3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> steps, the state is updated, and the process repeats. This interleaved planning and execution ensures adaptation, persistent collision avoidance, and progress towards goals <math id="S3.SS3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\bm{p}_{i}^{\text{goal}}\}_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>goal</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\bm{p}_{i}^{\text{goal}}\}_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math>. Executing up to <math id="S3.SS3.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> provides a balance between reactivity and planning efficiency, avoiding the excessive planning time of single-step execution.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Experiments</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our experiments aim to answer the following key questions regarding DG-MAP:</p>
<ul id="S4.I1" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="S4.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S4.I1.ix1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Q1:</span></span> 
<div id="S4.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">How effectively does DG-MAP scale to planning for larger numbers of arms (<math id="S4.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=3</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.I1.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=8</annotation></semantics></math>) when trained only on single and dual-arm interaction data?</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S4.I1.ix2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Q2:</span></span> 
<div id="S4.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">How does DG-MAP’s performance compare to the learning-based methods, trained on limited interaction data?</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.ix3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S4.I1.ix3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Q3:</span></span> 
<div id="S4.I1.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.I1.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Can DG-MAP remain competitive with the learning-based methods, which leverage significantly more complex higher-order interaction data during training?</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.ix4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S4.I1.ix4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Q4:</span></span> 
<div id="S4.I1.ix4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.ix4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Can DG-MAP be applied to practical applications apart from simple single goal-reaching tasks?</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F3" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="S4.F3.fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.08160v1/figures/easy.png" id="S4.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/268;" width="476" height="268" alt="Refer to caption">
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="S4.F3.fig2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.08160v1/figures/medium.png" id="S4.F3.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/268;" width="476" height="268" alt="Refer to caption">
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="S4.F3.fig3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.08160v1/figures/hard.png" id="S4.F3.g3" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/268;" width="476" height="268" alt="Refer to caption">
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 3: </span>Visualization of test tasks for four arms across different difficulty levels: easy (left), medium (middle), and hard (right). Task difficulty is based on the maximum intersection between the arms’ hemispherical workspaces <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>, with easy tasks involving minimal arm interaction and hard tasks requiring significant overlap and coordination.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Setup:</span> We focus on static single goal-reaching tasks with <math id="S4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=3</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=8</annotation></semantics></math> manipulator arms, forming a foundation for applications like pick-and-place. Each arm has <math id="S4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}=6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}=6</annotation></semantics></math> DoF. Tasks are executed in the PyBullet simulator <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>]</cite> and are considered successful if all <math id="S4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> arms reach their target end-effector poses <math id="S4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{p}_{i}^{\text{goal}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>goal</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{p}_{i}^{\text{goal}}</annotation></semantics></math> within a positional tolerance <math id="S4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\text{pos}}=0.03" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mtext>pos</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.03</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\text{pos}}=0.03</annotation></semantics></math> units and orientation tolerance <math id="S4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\text{rot}}=0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mtext>rot</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\text{rot}}=0.1</annotation></semantics></math> radians. Each attempt is limited to 400 simulation steps. We generate a test dataset of 18,000 unique scenarios, with novel base poses <math id="S4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\xi}_{i}^{\text{base}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝝃</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>base</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\xi}_{i}^{\text{base}}</annotation></semantics></math> and target poses <math id="S4.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{p}_{i}^{\text{goal}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>goal</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{p}_{i}^{\text{goal}}</annotation></semantics></math> distinct from training data, evenly distributed across arm counts. Following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>, tasks are categorized by difficulty based on the maximum workspace intersection volume between pairs of arms, as illustrated in the Figure <a href="#S4.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Diffusion-Guided Multi-Arm Motion Planning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. Implementation specific details can be found in the Appendix.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For comparisons, we utilize two variants of the multi-arm motion planner from Ha et al. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>, which represents a valuable learning-based baseline with demonstrable scalability assurances.</p>
<ol id="S4.I2" class="ltx_enumerate ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="S4.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S4.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Baseline-LD (Limited Data):</span> This variant is trained using only single-arm and dual-arm interactions for up to 756.8M timesteps. This comparison directly assesses the effectiveness of our approach given the same limited interaction data.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S4.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Baseline-ED (Extended Data):</span> This variant is trained on extended interaction including three and four arms for up to 668.2 M timesteps allowing us to quantify the performance differential between models that can leverage complex multi-arm coordination compared to simplistic pairwise interactions combined with planning.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Comparison with Baseline-LD:</span> Table <a href="#S4.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Diffusion-Guided Multi-Arm Motion Planning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> shows that DG-MAP significantly outperforms Baseline-LD across all task difficulties and team sizes. While Baseline-LD achieves moderate success with 3 arms (41.2% on average), its performance quickly deteriorates with more arms, dropping below 10% and sometimes failing entirely on medium and hard tasks beyond 4 arms. In contrast, DG-MAP maintains consistently high average success rates above 90% across all settings. This stark contrast highlights the scalability of DG-MAP’s planning-guided coordination in complex multi-arm environments, where learning-only methods like Baseline-LD struggle due to limited training on higher-order interactions addressing both <span id="S4.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold">Q1</span> and <span id="S4.p4.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold">Q2</span>.</p>
</div>
